            which is in addition equipped with operations that behave as the operations of forming
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+powers"} exterior powers
            (of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^n
            for the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+power"} exterior power
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+groups"} symmetric groups
          %p
            Equivalently, it turns out (
            %a{:href => "#Wilkerson82"}> Wilkerson 82
            ) that a
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
            that lifts the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+endomorphism"} Frobenius endomorphism
            after reduction mod
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            at each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borger%27s+absolute+geometry"} Borger's absolute geometry
            and are related, in some way, to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+operations"} power operations
            (see there for more) in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
          %h3#motivation_from_representation_theory Motivation from representation theory
          %p
            Typically one can form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebraic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            then inherits the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            — the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
          %p
            In many situations, we can also take
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor products
            of representations. Then the Grothendieck group becomes something better than an abelian group. It becomes a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+power"} exterior
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+power"} symmetric
            powers of representations; indeed, we can often apply any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+diagram"} Young diagram
            to a representation and get a new representation. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            becomes something better than a ring: it becomes a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                \-ring
          %p
            More generally, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            is always a ring, called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+ring"} Grothendieck ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided monoidal
            abelian category, this ring is commutative. But if we start with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            abelian category, we get a
            = succeed "-ring." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
          %p
            So,
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorify"} decategorify
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            — for example the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundles
            on a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            Unsurprisingly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
            of the free symmetric monoidal abelian category on one generator is the free
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur+functor"} Schur functors
            %em any
            symmetric monoidal abelian category. The irreducible objects in this category are called ‘Young diagrams’. Elements of the free
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+function"} symmetric functions
          %h3#in_terms_of_universal_algebra In terms of universal algebra
          %p
            A
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              \-ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/P-ring"} P-ring
            presented by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Symm
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mn 1
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Symm=\mathbb{Z}[h_1,h_1\dots]
            in countably many indeterminates over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integers
            or, equivalently,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Symm
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Symm
            is the ring of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+function"} symmetric functions
            in countably many
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copresheaf"} copresheaf
            presented by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Symm
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Symm
            such that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} CRing
                      %mo →
                      %mi CRing
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L:\CRing \to CRing
                defines an endofunctor on the category of commutative rings.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                gives rise to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mi Ring
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C Ring
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-action"} co-action
            of this comonad. As always is the case with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monads
            and comonads this definition can be formulated in terms of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#the_orthodox_definition The “orthodox” definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                \-structure
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative unital ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is defined to be a sequence of maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda^n
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge 0
              satisfying
            %ol
              %li
